---
import BlogArticleShell from '../../../components/BlogArticleShell.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonicalPath = '/blog/spreadsheet-wrong-variant-recovery-2026';
const publishedISO = '2026-07-03';
---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Wrong color or size shipped: spreadsheet variant recovery (2026) | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="Warehouse QC shows the wrong colourway or size versus your Kakobuy order? A 2026 editorial guide to variant mistakes—reject timing, seller exchange, re-order workflow, and prevention at paste time."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Wrong variant recovery: when spreadsheet rows arrive as a different colour or size (2026)"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="3 July 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'wrong variant Kakobuy recovery',
    'wrong color size agent 2026',
    'spreadsheet variant mistake',
    'warehouse QC exchange reps',
    'kakobuy-cn.com order recovery',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    You pasted the right <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> URL, selected EU 43 and Black/White, approved QC photos that looked fine—then the warehouse tag reads EU 42 and University Blue.
    Wrong-variant shipments are among the most fixable agent problems if you act early, and among the most expensive if you approve export anyway.
    This guide is editorial context for <strong>2026</strong> recovery—not a guarantee of seller cooperation.
  </p>

  <h2>Variant failure types</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Failure</th><th scope="col">Usually caused by</th><th scope="col">First action</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Wrong size</td><td>Seller pick error, listing SKU chaos</td><td>Reject before export; photo tag vs order</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wrong colourway</td><td>Thumbnail reuse, batch swap</td><td>Reject; compare to listing stills</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wrong model entirely</td><td>Dead link redirect, malicious swap</td><td>Reject + dispute; audit seller—<a href="/blog/spotting-red-flag-sellers-community-spreadsheets/">red flags</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Right variant, bad QC photos</td><td>Angle/lighting</td><td>Retake—not reject—<a href="/blog/qc-retake-reject-decision-spreadsheet-2026/">QC decision guide</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Prevention at paste time</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Screenshot listing variant selector on Taobao/Weidian before order.</li>
    <li>Double-check Kakobuy cart line matches colour/size characters—not just thumbnail.</li>
    <li>Use <a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">URL hygiene</a>; avoid shortened or redirected links.</li>
    <li>On apparel, note size chart row—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">sizing guide</a>.</li>
    <li>Prefer sellers with stable variant SKUs on repeat orders.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Recovery workflow inside Kakobuy</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Do not approve export</strong> if tag contradicts order—approval often limits options.</li>
    <li>Upload side-by-side: order screenshot vs warehouse tag vs listing.</li>
    <li>Request exchange or domestic return per agent UI policy.</li>
    <li>If seller refuses, reject and re-order from alternate row—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-domestic-returns-before-international-ship/">domestic returns</a>.</li>
    <li>Document for whitelist/blacklist decisions on future hauls.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Kakobuy policy details live in their signed-in help—we explain buyer sequencing, not legal outcomes.
  </p>

  <h2>Category-specific variant traps</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Sneakers:</strong> colourway names differ by region—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-sneakers-spreadsheet-lane-guide-2026/">sneakers lane</a>.
    <strong>Denim:</strong> wash codes vary—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-jeans-denim-spreadsheet-lane-2026/">jeans guide</a>.
    <strong>Bags:</strong> hardware colour variants—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-bags-spreadsheet-lane-guide-2026/">bags guide</a>.
    <strong>Jewelry:</strong> gold vs silver buckles—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-jewelry-watches-spreadsheet-lane-2026/">jewelry lane</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>When recovery fails</h2>
  <p>
    Some sellers stonewall; domestic return fees may exceed item value on budget rows.
    Cut losses early, blacklist URL, and post factual QC notes for community—<a href="/blog/community-crowdsourced-qc-verification-batches/">crowdsourced verification</a>.
    Insurance rarely covers variant errors—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-shipping-insurance-seizure-protection-guide/">insurance guide</a> covers different failures.
  </p>

  <h2>Bottom line</h2>
  <p>
    Variant mistakes are QC problems before they are freight problems.
    The spreadsheet got you to a row; paste discipline and early rejection protect haul #2 and #3—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-second-haul-spreadsheet-strategy-2026/">second haul playbook</a>.
  </p>
</BlogArticleShell>
